<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Cleartext policy lives in app code, not here.

    Android's network-security-config supports neither ranges nor wildcards, so
    "permit HTTP to any private-LAN address" cannot be expressed in this file.
    What used to be here instead was a hand-written list of fourteen private IPs
    — which matched a real user's LAN address only by coincidence, and which a
    user of an installed release build cannot edit. Running a local Ollama or
    MCP server over HTTP, the scenario this product is built around, therefore
    did not work for most people.

    Cleartext is permitted here so the rule can be expressed where it is
    expressible: `domain/services/CleartextPolicy.kt`. That rule is strictly
    narrower than "permit everything" — unencrypted traffic is allowed only to a
    loopback / private-LAN address the user has explicitly approved, and never
    to a public host — and it is enforced at every point that opens a connection
    to a user-configured address:

      * ModelNetworkGate.ollamaRefusal()  — the Ollama endpoint, asked by both
                                           KoogClientFactory (chat) and
                                           OllamaEmbeddingProvider (memory)
      * McpConnectionPool                  — every MCP connection
      * CleartextGuardInterceptor          — the shared OkHttp client, per request

    The trade-off (the platform no longer blocks a cleartext redirect inside the
    third-party Koog / Ktor stacks) is recorded in `project_docs/decisions.md`.
-->
<network-security-config xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <!--
        `InsecureBaseConfiguration` is suppressed deliberately, not silenced: the
        header above is the reasoning, and the alternative (a hard-coded address
        list) did not work for the scenario the product exists to support. It is
        suppressed here rather than in `lint-baseline.xml` so the justification
        stays next to the setting instead of in a file nobody reads.
    -->
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" tools:ignore="InsecureBaseConfiguration">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
